From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:55:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] cuda: ggml_cuda_pool_peer_copy_ok() for builds without
 VMM (r347 link error with -DGGML_HIP_NO_VMM=ON)

r347 (crash #373) defines ggml_cuda_pool_peer_copy_ok() inside #if defined(GGML_USE_VMM) in ggml-cuda.cu, while
ggml_cuda_peer_copy_ok() in ggml-cuda-slab.cu calls it unconditionally, so a -DGGML_HIP_NO_VMM=ON build fails to
link (undefined reference from libggml-hip.so; stock r349 fails identically).  Without VMM there is no pool range
whose peer grants could be incomplete, so the non-VMM definition answers true and the slab's own check decides.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
index 26b85ab65e..3250c02f05 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
@@ -1319,6 +1319,16 @@ struct ggml_cuda_pool_leg : public ggml_cuda_pool {
 };
 
 // pool with virtual memory
+#if !defined(GGML_USE_VMM)
+// No VMM pool in this build (e.g. -DGGML_HIP_NO_VMM=ON), so no pool range can have incomplete peer grants; the slab's
+// ggml_cuda_peer_copy_ok() still asks, so answer here rather than leave the symbol undefined.
+bool ggml_cuda_pool_peer_copy_ok(const void * dst, size_t nbytes) {
+    GGML_UNUSED(dst);
+    GGML_UNUSED(nbytes);
+    return true;
+}
+#endif
+
 #if defined(GGML_USE_VMM)
 // TRIAGE switch for the VMM pool's free-order invariant (`GGML_CUDA_POOL_TRACE=1`).  Off by default: it costs
 // a backtrace per temporary allocation.
-- 
